{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>שופטים</b> Judges adjoins Festivals, to teach that the Festivals depend on the judges. Also, for they must act to bring vows at the Festivals, as we say: a warning from the court that they must do so. Also, for the judges warn the people not to sin at the Festivals, as we say: the eve of the year is a festival:" "<b> כברכת ה' אלהיך אשר נתן לך</b> י שופטים. That the judges were commanded to give to one who is poor. Another interpretation: אשר נתן לך — שופטים, meaning: give to the judges, as it is said: לתת מנת וגו' למען יחזקו בתורת ה'." "<b> איש כמתנת ידו</b> שופטים. A hint that they pledge collateral for charity." "<b> שלש פעמים</b> and adjoined to it שופטים — that a person is obligated to greet his master at the Festival." "<b> שופטים</b> in gematria 70 — Sanhedrin. שפטים. בג. 40 sorcerers — that they appoint as judges masters of sorcery who know how to nullify sorceries. שופטים. Tags above and below — let the judge see as if a sword is above and Gehenna is open below." "<b> תתן לך</b> and not to a gentile. מגיד דבריו ליעקב חקיו ומשפטיו לישראל — חקיו ומשפטיו in gematria דיוקי משפטיו." "<b> בכל שעריך</b> In all that you assess your fellow's money, whether for taxes or to allocate to charity." "<b> לשבטיך ושפטו</b> To teach that it is a mitzvah for a judge to judge his own tribe. ושפטו. Letters ופשוט. Which is dearer to you — a case of פשוט, to scrutinize it like a case of a hundred maneh. שופטים. ושפטו. משפט. Behold three — thus monetary cases are by three."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {7 "The phrase 'Letters ופשוט' appears to mean that the letters of ושפטו, rearranged, form ופשוט; the argument then contrasts a 'simple' (פשוט) case with a large-sum case. The text 'הי חביב עליך' is rendered hyper-literally; 'הי' appears defective or abbreviated."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:59.319194754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}